{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo defects found. The guard preserves paths, base selection, and error behavior without mutating the retained graph. Probe caching matches R3; actual process termination remains independently verified.\n\nReviewed bundle `rvb-18aeaa6c0a46a548` against R1–R3 and D1. Applied security, backend-go, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Repository remains unchanged; no attestation recorded.\n\nTests were inspected and assessed using sealed evidence, without rebuilding in the read-only sandbox. The reported performance improvement remains a noisy measurement from two alternating runs.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified immutable graph reads, separate pointer-slice sorting, equivalent selection, and uncached termination verification. The spec explicitly accepts availability reporting remaining stale for up to one minute. The reported timing improvement is supported by two alternating runs but is not a statistically established performance guarantee.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-guard-reads-the-integrity-graph-in-place-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"review_dispatch_unix.go:134-144 protects timestamp reads, refresh, and publication with one mutex. Warm calls avoid inventory traversal; cold calls serialize it. Cache views pin retained entries and the guard writes only its local pointer slice and output. Actual cancellation and termination verification are unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"idleder\": \"unused\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
